"""Build the offline exact-state research page; standard library only."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent

def math(tex,display=False):
    return f'<span class="math{" display" if display else ""}" data-tex="{escape(tex,quote=True)}">{escape(tex)}</span>'

def links(folder,items):
    return '<div class="links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{folder}/{file}">{label} ↓</a>' for file,label in items)+'</div>'

def main():
    certlinks=[('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Exact certificate'),
        ('verify_independently.py','Portable independent verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Exact verification report')]
    text='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>23 and 25 qubits · Exact AC states and bounds</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>main{max-width:1050px;padding-block:40px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,48px)}h2{margin-top:40px}.display{display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:12px 0}.links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 20px;margin-block:20px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.claim{padding:18px 22px;background:var(--paper-alt,#f0efe9);border-left:3px solid var(--accent,#5e4b7c)}pre{overflow-x:auto;padding:14px;background:var(--paper-alt,#f0efe9)}section{scroll-margin-top:24px}</style></head><body><main><a href="../../index.html">← Pure AC-state catalogue</a><p class="eyebrow">Exact existence · Proven exclusions</p><h1>Twenty-three and twenty-five qubits</h1><p class="claim">The maximum pure AC order at N=23 is proved to be five. At N=25 an explicit radical state attains order five, and an exact four-copy partial-transpose certificate excludes order six. Both maxima are proved.</p>'''
    text+='<table><thead><tr><th>Qubits</th><th>Exact attained order</th><th>Rigorous maximum order</th><th>Construction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>23</th><td>5</td><td>'+math(r't_{\max}(23)=5')+'</td><td>Certified exact algebraic root</td></tr><tr><th>25</th><td>5</td><td>'+math(r't_{\max}(25)=5')+'</td><td>Six Dicke components; explicit radicals</td></tr></tbody></table>'
    text+='<section id="n23"><h2>23 qubits: certified maximum order five</h2><p>The exact state is defined by a unique algebraic root near the refined Liège numerical state:</p>'+math(r'|\psi_{23}\rangle=\sum_{r=0}^{23}\frac{\sqrt{\binom{23}{r}}}{d_r}(x_r^*+ix_{24+r}^*)|D_{23}^{(r)}\rangle.',True)
    text+='<p>The certificate records 48 real coordinates, positive integer scales '+math(r'd_r')+', a rational center, and 12 coordinates fixed to their central values. The other 36 coordinates are the unique real zero in the stated box of the rational quadratic equations equivalent to '+math(r'\rho_5=I_6/6')+'. This is an exact implicit algebraic definition; closed-form radical components are not claimed.</p>'
    text+='<h3>Existence from a rational contraction</h3><p>For the 36 active variables, set '+math(r'T(y)=y-AF(y)')+'. Exact rational arithmetic verifies</p>'+math(r'\begin{gathered}r=10^{-65},\quad\|AF(y^0)\|_\infty<4\cdot10^{-66},\\\|I-ADF(y^0)\|_\infty<10^{-76},\quad\|A\|_\infty<1600,\\H\le2^{20},\qquad q<10^{-55},\qquad\|AF(y^0)\|_\infty+qr<r.\end{gathered}',True)
    text+='<p>Banach’s theorem supplies a unique fixed point in the box. The inverse-defect bound makes '+math(r'A')+' invertible, so the fixed point satisfies '+math(r'F=0')+'. Its nonsingular rational polynomial system makes the coordinates algebraic. The identity reduction proves exact normalization. Every real or imaginary Dicke component is within '+math(r'2\cdot10^{-65}')+' of the exact rational-center conversion. Floating components and copied nearby Majorana points are numerical renderings.</p>'
    text+='<h3>Why order six is impossible</h3><p>An exact four-copy positivity certificate excludes every sixth-order pure symmetric state on 23 qubits. For a hypothetical state, its rotationally averaged four-copy projector is positive, has trace one, and satisfies necessary low-multipole contraction equations. A coefficientwise rational separating identity with positive-definite certificate matrices gives a contradiction. This applies to arbitrary complex states without restricting their support or constellation symmetry. Together with the certified fifth-order state, it proves the maximum five.</p><p><a href="../../index.html#n=23&amp;t=5&amp;state=certified-algebraic-n23-t5">Open the certified state and its Majorana sphere ↗</a></p>'
    text+=links('n23-t5',certlinks)+'<h3>Universal sixth-order exclusion</h3>'+links('n23-t6',certlinks)+'</section>'

    text+='<section id="n25"><h2>25 qubits: an explicit exactly fifth-order state</h2><p>Set</p>'+math(r'w=\frac{1001-i\sqrt{1561327}}{16\sqrt{10013}},\qquad|w|=1.',True)
    formula=r'\begin{aligned}|\psi_{25}\rangle={}&\sqrt{\frac{21}{250}}\bigl(|D_{25}^{(0)}\rangle-|D_{25}^{(25)}\rangle\bigr)\\&-i\sqrt{\frac{31}{125}}\bigl(|D_{25}^{(5)}\rangle-|D_{25}^{(20)}\rangle\bigr)\\&-iw\sqrt{\frac{21}{125}}\bigl(|D_{25}^{(10)}\rangle-|D_{25}^{(15)}\rangle\bigr).\end{aligned}'
    text+=math(formula,True)
    text+='<p>The normalized Dicke probabilities '+math(r'(21,62,42,42,62,21)/250')+' match the uniform spin moments through degree five. Support gaps eliminate shifts one through four; the exact phase '+math(r'w')+' cancels the remaining fifth coherence. Independent symbolic partial traces verify</p>'+math(r'\rho_5=I_6/6,\qquad(\rho_6)_{00}-1/7=\frac{13}{35420}\ne0.',True)
    text+='<p>This representative is exactly fifth-order AC and has proper dihedral '+math(r'D_5')+' symmetry. An exact reciprocal-polynomial discriminant calculation proves that all 25 Majorana stars are distinct.</p><p><a href="../../index.html#n=25&amp;t=5&amp;state=radical-n25-t5">Open the radical state and its Majorana sphere ↗</a></p>'
    text+=links('n25-t5',[('proof.tex','Analytical construction'),('states.json','Exact radical Dicke components'),('build_witness.py','Portable construction'),('verify_witness.py','Independent direct-trace verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Exact verification report')])
    text+='<h3>Why order five is globally maximal</h3><p>An exact four-copy certificate excludes every sixth-order pure symmetric state. The rotationally averaged four-copy moment must satisfy the AC contraction equations and have positive partial transposes across both the one–three and two–two splits. An exact rational separating identity contradicts trace one.</p><p>The portable verifier reconstructs the physical input representation, the contraction rows, both partial-transpose maps and every positivity check. The proof covers arbitrary complex states without restricting support or constellation symmetry. Together with the radical witness, it proves '+math(r't_{\max}(25)=5')+'.</p>'
    text+=links('n25-t6',[('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX maximum-order proof'),('source-identity.json','Exact rational separating identity'),('rational-cuts.json','Exact partial-transpose vectors'),('verify_independently.py','Portable independent verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Exact verification report'),('certificate-bundle.zip','Complete proof and verifier bundle')])
    text+='<p>The earlier <a href="n25-t7/proof.tex">three-copy seventh-order exclusion</a> is retained as an auxiliary result; the sixth-order exclusion closes the previous gap.</p>'

    text+='<section id="reproduce"><h2>Reproduce the proofs offline</h2><p>The N25 radical witness scripts require SymPy. The N23 contraction and exclusion verifiers, including the complete N25 fourth-copy exclusion, require only Python’s standard library, with their certificate files beside them. Download the complete N25 proof bundle to obtain all helper files.</p><pre><code>python3 n23-t5/verify_independently.py\npython3 n23-t6/verify_independently.py\npython3 n25-t5/build_witness.py\npython3 n25-t5/verify_witness.py\npython3 n25-t6/verify_independently.py</code></pre><p>The optional <a href="n23-t5/build.py">N23 discovery script</a> accepts <code>--source</code>. Numerical discovery is separate from the exact verifier.</p><div class="links"><a href="states.json">Combined state records ↓</a><a href="build_states.py">Rebuild the records ↓</a><a href="build_page.py">Rebuild this page ↓</a><a href="../n24-n26/index.html">Exact maxima at N=24 and N=26 ↗</a></div></section></main><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>{for(const el of document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]"))katex.render(el.dataset.tex,el,{displayMode:el.classList.contains("display"),throwOnError:true});});</script></body></html>'
    (HERE/'index.html').write_text(text)
    print('Built offline page: proved maximum5 at N23 and N25.')

if __name__=='__main__':main()
